{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ושמור נפשך", :translit "u'sh'mor naf'shekha", :gloss "and guard your soul"} {:he "נר אלהים נשמת אדם", :translit "ner elohim nishmat adam", :gloss "the lamp of God is the soul of man"} {:he "נרך בידי ונרי בידך אם תשמור נרי אשמור נרך", :translit "nerkha b'yadi v'nri b'yadekha im tish'mor nri ash'mor nerkha", :gloss "your lamp is in My hand and My lamp is in your hand, if you guard My lamp I will guard your lamp"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: נפשך (your soul) read through the lens of נר אלהים נשמת אדם (Proverbs 20:27)"}], :frame {:text "Proverbs 20:27 states נר אלהים נשמת אדם, 'the lamp of the LORD is the soul of man.' The verse ושמור נפשך ('take heed to your soul') is thus read as a charge to guard one's soul, which is God's lamp. The reciprocal formulation — 'Your lamp is in My hand and My lamp is in your hand; if you guard My lamp I will guard your lamp' — echoes the talmudic principle of reciprocal divine-human obligation articulated at Shabbat 31a.", :sources ["Proverbs 20:27" "Shabbat 31a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והודעתם לבניך ולבני בניך", :translit "v'hoda'tam l'vanekha u'l'vnei vanekha", :gloss "and you shall make them known to your children and your children's children"} {:he "שלשה נוני\"ן הפוכין", :translit "shloshah nunin hafukhin", :gloss "three inverted nuns"} {:he "שכל מי שהוא ובנו ובן בנו תלמידי חכמים שוב אין התורה פוסקת מזרעו", :translit "shekhol mi shehu u'vno u'ven beno talmidei chachamim shuv ein ha'torah poskelet mi'zaro", :gloss "that anyone who is himself and his son and his son's son Torah scholars, the Torah does not cease from his seed"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Masoretic observation: three inverted nun letters in the phrase correspond to three generations (you, your son, your son's son)"}], :frame {:text "The Sifrei on Devarim 34 states that if a person, his son, and his grandson are all Torah scholars, the Torah never ceases from their descendants. The Ba'al HaTurim links this tradition to three inverted nun letters found in this phrase, each nun representing one generation in the chain of transmission.", :sources ["Sifrei Devarim 34"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: נפשך (your soul) read through the lens of נר אלהים נשמת אדם (Proverbs 20:27)", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Masoretic observation: three inverted nun letters in the phrase correspond to three generations (you, your son, your son's son)", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:33:58.193990224Z", :model "glm-5.2"}